  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**  \n   The Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem seeks to minimize the maximum overlap between a step function and its shifted versions. We enhance the search strategy by decomposing the optimization into sparse/dense subproblems and introducing efficient warming-up phases. The core idea is:  \n   - Start with sparse solutions (minimal support) at low resolutions  \n   - Progressively add support via multi-dimensional search  \n   - Temperature-based geometric programming resolves combinatorial issues  \n   This addresses local optimization traps by leveraging sparse initialization and dimensionality reduction, resulting in faster convergence to global minima.  \n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**  \n   - **Objective**: Minimize \\( C\u2085 = \\max_k \\int_0\u00b2 h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx \\)  \n   - **Constraints**: \\( 0 \\leq h(x) \\leq 1 \\), \\( \\int_0\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1 \\)  \n   - **Representation**: Piecewise constant with variable support. For resolution \\( N \\), domain \\([0, 2]\\), define \\( h(x) \\) by \\( M \\) interior points \\( t_j \\) (sorted) and values \\( h_j \\) (discrete differences).  \n   - **Hierarchical Optimization**:\n     - Sparse layer: \\( M = \\log_2 (N/4) \\)  \n     - Medium layer: \\( M = 0.2 \\times \\log N \\)  \n     - Dense layer: Full support \\( h \\)  \n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**  \n   **Parent Initialization**:\n   - Input: `initial_h_values` parent solution  \n   - Resample to test resolution \\( N = 128 \\) (down to limit)  \n   - Project with clipping/enforcement: `project_h(parent, target_sum=N/2)`  \n\n   **Sparse Exploration**:\n   - Start at \\( M = 10 \\) points, current distribution \\( t_j \\) uniform  \n   - Compute medium-scale representation \\( h(x) = a_j \\prod_{k=1}^T (1 - |x - t_k| / b_j) \\)  \n   - Enforce integrals via: \\( adjust_support(h, tol=1e-3) \\)  \n   - Evaluate \\( C\u2085 \\) using:  \n     `compute_c5(h)`  \n\n   **Medium-Density Expansion**:\n   - Add 2 points per step, using Voronoi repulsion:  \n     `t_{j+new} = t_j + \\epsilon_j * (random - 0.5)`  \n   - Ensure mass conservation: `normalize_mass(h, target_sum)`  \n\n   **Geometric Programming**:\n   - Stage-wise optimization:  \n     I. Initialize \\( N = 128 \\)  \n     II. Lower-temperature iterations (\\( \\tau = 0.5 \\)): Safer move acceptance  \n     III. Geometric programming (BP) relaxation:  \n          \\( \\text{minimize} \\sum_{k} p_k \\| h + s_k + a_k \\|^2 \\)  \n          via Mosek / CPLEX solution handlers  \n\n   **Termination**:\n   - Candidates stored with \\( \\|h\\|_\u221e \\leq 1 \\) and \\( \\int h = N/2 \\)  \n   - Evaluate populations on full \\( N=384 \\) grid  \n\n   **Fallbacks**:  \n   - If SLP/QP fails, use `cvxpy` with DCP-compliant template:  \n     ```\n     p = Program(Minimize(objective), [0.2*norm2(h_obj-1), \n                                       0.3*sum(h),\n                                       h \u2265 0, h \u2264 1])\n     ```\n   - Rescue from NaN: Clip states explicitly  \n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**  \n   - **Sparse vs Dense**:\n     - Use sparse auto-detection: \\( M = \\floor{0.3 \\times \\min(\\log N, 20)} \\)  \n     - Adaptive hierarchy: \\( M_i = M_{i-1} + 3 \\) if fitness improvable  \n   - **Temperature Scheduling**:\n     - Start at \\( \\tau_{\\text{max}} \\), cool per iteration:  \n       \\( \\tau = \\tau \\times 0.995 \\)  \n     - If stuck, reset \\( \\tau \\) to 0.1  \n   - **Domain Decomposition**:\n     - Binary splits: Start with even distribution, then asymmetrical shifts  \n     - Hyperbolic decay for gradient weight:  \n       \\( w(x) = \\frac{1}{1 + c \\cdot x} \\)  \n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**  \n   - **Estimation**:  \n     - Sparse optimization: \\( O(N \\log N) \\)  \n     - Geometric programming: \\( O(100 \\text{ s per problem}) \\)  \n     - Cooldown: 40 iter/sec (actual values for \\( \\tau \\) cooling)  \n   - **Feasibility**:\n     - Time limit: Check at \\( T/4 \\), \\( T/2 \\), \\( T \\cdot 3/4 \\)  \n     - Fallback path: `parent_best = initial_h_values`  \n     - NaN detection: Wrap `np.clip` + `finite_check`  \n   - **Resource Use**:  \n     - Avoid `sum`/`clip` with intermediate NaNs  \n     - Use `np.errstate` to mask invalid operations  \n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**  \n   - **Pre-checks**:  \n     ```\n     def validate_candidate(h):  \n         if any(~np.isfinite(h)): return False, None  \n         if sum(abs(h-0), 1))<1e-6: # All zeros/outliers  \n             project_h(h, 1.0) if T-t0>0.5 else None  \n         return True, h\n     ```  \n   - **Objective Safety**:\n     - `compute_c5` with gradient fallback:  \n       ```\n       try: return np.max(compute_c5(h))  \n       except: return float('inf')  \n       ```\n   - **Precision Constraints**:  \n     - Full resolution record kept for benchmarks  \n     - Early exit if current \\( C_5 + 1 \\geq \\text{previous best} \\)  \n     - Mass tolerance \\( 2 \\times 1/\\text{res} \\) allowed",
